data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant, Amit Kumar Sahu, son of Shri Birendra Sahu, aged 28 years, resident of"}

data: {"text":" House No. 14, Harmu Housing Colony, Ranchi - 834002, has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 78/2026 dated 01.04.2026, registered at Police Station Lalpur, under Sections"}

data: {"text":" 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, wherein Section 303 is"}

data: {"text":" non-bailable and Section 351 is bailable.\n\n2. That the present case arises out of a property dispute between the complainant and the Applicant's family,"}

data: {"text":" which has been pending for considerable time. The complainant, with"}

data: {"text":" malafide intentions and to pressurize the Applicant's family in the said"}

data: {"text":" property dispute, has falsely implicated the Applicant in the present case by lev"}

data: {"text":"eling false and concocted allegations against him.\n\n3. That the Applicant submits that he was not present at the alleged"}

data: {"text":" spot at the time of the incident in question and has CCTV evidence from a nearby shop which clearly establishes his presence elsewhere at the material"}

data: {"text":" time. The Applicant was arrested on 02.04.2026 and has been languishing in judicial custody since then, despite being innocent of the charges leveled against him."}

data: {"text":"\n\n4. That the Applicant is a law-abiding citizen with no criminal antecedents whatsoever and has never"}

data: {"text":" been involved in any criminal activity in the past. The Applicant has deep roots in the society and has been residing"}

data: {"text":" at the same address for years, thereby establishing that he poses no flight"}

data: {"text":" risk and will not abscond from the process of law.\n\n5. That the Applicant has been"}

data: {"text":" fully cooperating with the investigating agency since the beginning and has appeared"}

data: {"text":" before the police whenever called upon. The Applicant has never attempted to tamper with evidence or influence"}

data: {"text":" witnesses and has complete faith in the judicial system to deliver justice.\n\n6. That the continued detention of the Applicant in"}

data: {"text":" judicial custody is a violation of his fundamental right to life and personal liberty as guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of"}

data: {"text":" India, particularly when he has been falsely implicated in the present case and the investigation is pending"}

data: {"text":".\n\n7. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by any conditions that this Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Court may deem fit to impose upon him and will not misuse the liberty if granted bail. The Applicant further undertakes not"}

data: {"text":" to leave the jurisdiction of this Hon'ble Court without prior permission and will appear before the investigating agency as and when required.\n\n8. That there"}

data: {"text":" is no possibility of the Applicant tampering with evidence or influencing witnesses, as the CCTV evidence clearly establishes his innocence and presence elsewhere"}

data: {"text":" at the time of the alleged incident. The grant of bail to the Applicant will not prejudice the investigation in any manner.\n\n9. That the present application is being"}

data: {"text":" made bonafide and in the interest of justice, and the Applicant has not suppressed any material facts from this"}

data: {"text":" Hon'ble Court. The Applicant is confident that upon proper investigation, his innocence will be established and he will be acqu"}

data: {"text":"itted of all charges."}

